5. EXCLUSIONS — WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT GRANT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.1  The multi-vector optimisation solver engine referenced in the README
     ("what is deliberately not in this repository") is NOT part of this
     release, is NOT covered by either licence above, and is NOT granted
     here. It is protected as an industrial secret under a pending patent
     application. Access to it is available to reviewers under a
     confidential peer-review agreement, per the IEEE PES Data Availability
     policy. Nothing in this file grants any right in that engine, in any
     patent application covering it, or in any confidential material
     associated with it.

5.2  No trademark, service mark, logo or institutional name is granted by
     this licence. The names of the Universidad Politécnica de Valencia and
     of any other institution referenced in this release remain the property
     of their respective owners and are used for attribution only.

5.3  This licence does not, and cannot, certify the physical correctness of
     the released network model. The certified scope of the release is the
     internal consistency of the released arrays under the declared
     electrical identities, the condensed-solve invariants, and the eight
     canonical contingency balances — see the README section "Scope of the
     Verification Harness".

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. HOW TO VERIFY THIS RELEASE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every released artefact carries a SHA-512 signature. From the repository
root:

    sha512sum -c SHA512SUMS.txt
    for f in *.sha512; do sha512sum -c "$f"; done

The two commands cover the canonical manifest and the per-artefact sidecars
respectively; `MANIFIESTO_SHA512_R5_DEFINITIVO.txt` carries the third layer
(a signed changelog with an embedded hash block). See the README section
"Cryptographic Integrity Verification".
